## Building a Budget Tracker

### Transaction Types

```xiom
enum TransactionType {
  Income;
  Expense;
}

type Transaction {
  amount: Int;
  category: Str;
  description: Str;
  tx_type: TransactionType;
}
```

### Budget State

```xiom
type Budget {
  balance: Int;
  income_total: Int;
  expense_total: Int;
  transactions: Vec[Transaction];
}

fn create_budget() -> Budget {
  Budget{ balance: 0, income_total: 0, expense_total: 0, transactions: Vec[Transaction].new() }
}
```

### Recording Transactions

```xiom
fn add_income(budget: &mut Budget, amount: Int, category: Str, desc: Str) {
  budget.balance += amount;
  budget.income_total += amount;
  budget.transactions.push(Transaction{
    amount: amount, category: category,
    description: desc, tx_type: TransactionType.Income
  });
}

fn add_expense(budget: &mut Budget, amount: Int, category: Str, desc: Str) {
  budget.balance -= amount;
  budget.expense_total += amount;
  budget.transactions.push(Transaction{
    amount: amount, category: category,
    description: desc, tx_type: TransactionType.Expense
  });
}
```

### Category Summaries

```xiom
fn category_total(budget: &Budget, category: Str) -> Int {
  let mut total = 0;
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < budget.transactions.len() {
    let tx = budget.transactions.get(i).unwrap();
    if tx.category == category {
      total += tx.amount;
    };
    i += 1;
  };
  total
}
```

### Budget Report

```xiom
fn print_report(budget: &Budget) {
  io.println(budget.balance);
  io.println(budget.income_total);
  io.println(budget.expense_total);

  let savings = budget.income_total - budget.expense_total;
  io.println(savings);
}
```

### Common Categories

- Housing, Food, Transportation, Utilities, Entertainment, Healthcare, Savings

